  "intro": "Memorize the core derivatives: $\\frac{d}{dx}\\sin x=\\cos x$, $\\frac{d}{dx}\\cos x=-\\sin x$, $\\frac{d}{dx}\\tan x=\\sec^2 x$, $\\frac{d}{dx}e^x=e^x$, $\\frac{d}{dx}\\ln x=\\frac{1}{x}$, and $\\frac{d}{dx}a^x=a^x\\ln a$. Combine them with the product, quotient, and chain rules. For a composite such as $e^{g(x)}$ the chain rule gives $g'(x)e^{g(x)}$, and $\\frac{d}{dx}\\ln(g(x))=\\frac{g'(x)}{g(x)}$.",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 1,
      "prompt": "Differentiate $f(x)=e^x\\sin x$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Use the product rule with $u=e^x$ and $v=\\sin x$.",
          "$u'=e^x$ and $v'=\\cos x$.",
          "$f'=u'v+uv'=e^x\\sin x+e^x\\cos x=e^x(\\sin x+\\cos x)$."
        ],
        "answer": "$f'(x)=e^x(\\sin x+\\cos x)$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 2,
      "prompt": "Differentiate $f(x)=\\ln(x^2+1)$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Use $\\frac{d}{dx}\\ln(g)=\\frac{g'}{g}$ with $g=x^2+1$.",
          "Here $g'=2x$.",
          "So $f'(x)=\\dfrac{2x}{x^2+1}$."
        ],
        "answer": "$f'(x)=\\dfrac{2x}{x^2+1}$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 3,
      "prompt": "Differentiate $f(x)=e^{3x}\\cos x$ at the level of setting up the rules.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Product rule with $u=e^{3x}$, $v=\\cos x$.",
          "Chain rule gives $u'=3e^{3x}$; $v'=-\\sin x$.",
          "$f'=3e^{3x}\\cos x-e^{3x}\\sin x=e^{3x}(3\\cos x-\\sin x)$."
        ],
        "answer": "$f'(x)=e^{3x}(3\\cos x-\\sin x)$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 4,
      "prompt": "Differentiate $f(x)=\\sin(5x)$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Chain rule: $\\cos(5x)\\cdot 5=5\\cos(5x)$."
        ],
        "answer": "$f'(x)=5\\cos(5x)$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 5,
      "prompt": "Differentiate $f(x)=x^2 e^x$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Product rule: $2x\\,e^x+x^2 e^x=e^x(x^2+2x)$."
        ],
        "answer": "$f'(x)=e^x(x^2+2x)$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 6,
      "prompt": "Differentiate $f(x)=\\dfrac{\\sin x}{x}$ and simplify.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Quotient rule: $\\dfrac{x\\cos x-\\sin x}{x^2}$."
        ],
        "answer": "$f'(x)=\\dfrac{x\\cos x-\\sin x}{x^2}$"
      }
    }
